  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-12-03T01:40:41.046Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I expressed my refusal to have my official ID linked to my internet persona. It’s the whole point of not using my real name. And I was told that no information could link my ID to my account. But here we have “Once an ID has been used to verify one VRChat account, it cannot be used to verify other accounts (alts).”. That sounds tightly linked to me.\n\nIt says I can contact support to ahve my information deleted but \" If you ask us to remove all of your information from the VRChat servers, this may affect your Verification status or your account may become unusable.\" So the answer in reality is NO. I can’t.\n\nWe also have “You may also request that Persona delete your ID data at any time. This will not affect your Age Verification status.” versus “Some data must be stored with Persona while you maintain a Verified Account that lets us know if an ID has already been used.”\n\nI was reminded that the Privacy Doc from persona states that the information would be deleted IMMEDIATELY after verification or within 3 years. Which seemed confusing in itself, but here it is made worse “Persona will retain your ID data for as long as necessary to provide Age Verification for VRChat.”. It seems to indicate “Indefninitely while you have a VRC account.”\n\nNONE OF THIS is necessary. All this take is to verify ONCE, mark it in your database as “THIS GUY IS A VERIFIED ADULT”. Done. Delete everything else. Because people don’t get younger as time passes. That is not how nature works.",
